<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elective monarchy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as elected monarchy, elected kingship</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An elective monarchy is a system in which the monarch is chosen by election rather than inheriting the throne. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> the whole nobility could take part in electing the king, who had to accept conditions limiting his powers. The system protected noble liberties but invited foreign interference and weakened the state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elective-monarchy.jpg" alt="Elective monarchy" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernardo Bellotto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Election_of_Stanis%C5%82aw_August_Poniatowski_in_1764_(detail).PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
